{"journal_version":1,"sequence":9,"replace_from":11,"message_count":12,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Verification passed. Done. Report concisely.\n\nAlso maybe check diff—not necessary but quick? Budget fine. I'll just report.","content":"Done.\n\n**Change** — `src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`:\n- Extracted the simulated-delay scheduling into a `scheduleResult` callback backed by a `timerRef`, which clears any pending timer before starting a new one (prevents overlapping timers) and is cleared on unmount.\n- Added a `Retry sync` button (`button.secondary`, existing style) inside the error state. It sets state to `loading` immediately (`Checking service…`), then completes as `All changes are synced.` after the same 120 ms delay — no navigation/reload, and no interaction with task selection outside this component.\n- Success path at `/` and the initial error detection at `/?sync=error` are otherwise unchanged; the retry control is only rendered in the error branch, so it disappears after success.\n\n**Commands run**:\n- `verify_frontend` → `npm run verify:agent` = `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`) + `npm run test:public` (Playwright, 6 tests). Exit code 0; all 6 public tests passed.\n\n**Remaining risks**:\n- Retry always resolves to success by design (per acceptance criteria); no repeated-error retry path is modeled.\n- The public suite has no explicit test for the new retry button/timer behavior, so that flow is verified only by the build and code review.","response_items":[{"id":"76054783-7277-45ea-bf08-0e8f71c47079","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Verification passed. Done. Report concisely.\n\nAlso maybe check diff—not necessary but quick? Budget fine. I'll just report.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"fdf8da24-b2d7-4150-9c8d-2801840b0b26-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"faccd650-a6aa-46ce-afa3-5845bfcd308c","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Done.\n\n**Change** — `src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`:\n- Extracted the simulated-delay scheduling into a `scheduleResult` callback backed by a `timerRef`, which clears any pending timer before starting a new one (prevents overlapping timers) and is cleared on unmount.\n- Added a `Retry sync` button (`button.secondary`, existing style) inside the error state. It sets state to `loading` immediately (`Checking service…`), then completes as `All changes are synced.` after the same 120 ms delay — no navigation/reload, and no interaction with task selection outside this component.\n- Success path at `/` and the initial error detection at `/?sync=error` are otherwise unchanged; the retry control is only rendered in the error branch, so it disappears after success.\n\n**Commands run**:\n- `verify_frontend` → `npm run verify:agent` = `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`) + `npm run test:public` (Playwright, 6 tests). Exit code 0; all 6 public tests passed.\n\n**Remaining risks**:\n- Retry always resolves to success by design (per acceptance criteria); no repeated-error retry path is modeled.\n- The public suite has no explicit test for the new retry button/timer behavior, so that flow is verified only by the build and code review.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T16:06:59.036189+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":19456,"context_tokens":5437,"step_count":5,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["41a19181bbd813f18f2f604051ce7cea","54c6d4923513570e71525b862782cc14","0b2507d4e6e12b98774fdb7da83e9c8c","552310babe8c1512828246e5084d0619","3c45d71dcb1acaddc13d0e86e5418077"],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":true,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":5,"scout_ledger":[{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx (30 l